 "localized_name": "bit_depth"}, {"widget": {"name": "color_space"}, "shape": 7, "name": "color_space", "label": "color_space", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "color_space"}, {"widget": {"name": "codec"}, "shape": 7, "name": "codec", "label": "codec", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "codec"}], "flags": {}, "type": "CreateVideo", "title": "E5｜24fps合成 · 保留原生音频", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#1c322e", "size": [325, 165], "pos": [2270, 2290], "id": 220, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "widget_ue_connectable": {"codec": true, "fps": true, "bit_depth": true, "color_space": true}, "Node name for S&R": "CreateVideo"}, "order": 37}, {"outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "slot_index": 0, "links": [15], "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "字符串"}], "color": "#25465c", "widgets_values": ["For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1]\nLive-action luxury fashion campaign for the trench coat worn in the reference image. A 15-second, 16:9 widescreen commercial, with five precisely edited shots. The visual concept is a quiet human presence against an immense landscape, with the wind revealing the coat’s construction, weight, and silhouette.\n\nBegin exactly from the supplied image: the same woman positioned right of center on a black volcanic plain, walking toward screen right beneath a vast deep-blue twilight sky. Preserve the distant low mountains, the narrow warm glow along the right horizon, the textured volcanic ground, and the original direction of light. Her long dark hair, facial features, black boots, and pale warm-beige trench coat remain consistent throughout.\n\nThe trench coat is the sole advertised product. Preserve its exact length, shoulder shape, collar, sleeve proportions, waist belt, back construction, and softly structured silhouette from the image. Its matte woven surface catches light gently; substantial fabric forms broad, weighted folds rather than thin, fluttering wrinkles. Keep the belt tied in its original configuration. Do not introduce new buttons, decorative hardware, patterns, accessories, or branding.\n\nFrom the exact opening pose, she continues walking naturally toward screen right. The camera tracks alongside her, gradually moving closer while retaining the expansive sky and low horizon. Nearby volcanic stones move faster than the distant mountains, creating clear physical depth. Wind travels consistently from screen right toward screen left, carrying her hair, the loose belt ends, and the lower coat panels backward. The coat responds with a restrained, weighted movement, never flying horizontally.\n\nThe original blue-hour atmosphere remains unchanged. Cool ambient light shapes the shadows, while the faint warm light from the right separates the beige fabric from the dark terrain. Footsteps crunch softly against volcanic grit.\n\n[Shot 2]\nAt 00:03.000, the camera cuts to a close-up of the coat’s back waist and upper skirt as she continues walking.\n\nThe frame clearly reveals the existing belt knot, belt ends, seam placement, and the fabric gathering naturally beneath the waist. The camera glides a short distance sideways along the garment, with shallow depth of field separating the pale fabric from the dark landscape.\n\nA gentle gust lifts one loose belt end, then lets it settle. Below the belt, a broad fold travels through the coat as her next step places tension on the fabric. Low, grazing light reveals fine woven texture, neat stitching, and soft tonal changes across the folds. The belt remains secure and unchanged.\n\nFocus stays on real tailoring and fabric behavior. No disassembly, transparent fabric, artificial glowing seams, or invented performance graphics. A close, soft fabric rustle accompanies the movement.\n\n[Shot 3]\nAt 00:05.500, the camera cuts on the backward sweep of the hem to a low, full-length side tracking shot.\n\nThe woman takes two measured strides across the black ground. Her complete coat remains visible from collar to hem, with her black boots grounding the silhouette. The camera travels parallel to her at approximately knee height; rough foreground stones pass close to the lens while the horizon stays level.\n\nThe long coat panels separate slightly with each step, then fall back under their own weight. The waist remains defined, the shoulder line stays composed, and the sleeves retain their original shape. Her posture is upright and effortless, without exaggerated runway posing.\n\nA slightly stronger gust creates one clean backward sweep of the lower coat, briefly revealing the depth and movement of its existing panels. The pale silhouette stands out sharply against the nearly black landscape. Her pace remains natural; the impact comes from low perspective, foreground parallax, and the movement of the garment, not running or frantic editing.\n\n[Shot 4]\nAt 00:08.500, the camera cuts to a closer three-quarter rear view as she finishes her stride and comes to a natural stop.\n\nThe camera makes a smooth, approximately 40-degree arc toward her side profile, beginning with purposeful movement and easing gently to a stop. Frame her from head to below the coat hem, keeping the garment large and clearly readable. The distant mountain ridge shifts behind her through genuine camera parallax.\n\nShe lifts her chin slightly toward the warm horizon. Her expression remains composed; she does not turn to address the viewer or perform a promotional gesture.\n\nA single sustained gust passes from right to left. In a restrained slow-motion moment, her hair moves first, followed by the loose belt ends and then a broad wave through the lower coat. The fabric opens away from her legs only moderately, showing its generous cut and weight before settling. Her shoulders, waist, and stance remain stable.\n\nThe existing warm side light catches the collar edge, sleeve contour, and raised folds while the cool sky maintains detail in the shadows. This is the visual climax: the coat’s pale, sculptural form moving against an immense dark landscape. No sudden sunrise, supernatural light beam, dust explosion, or change of location.\n\n[Shot 5]\nAt 00:12.000, the camera cuts to the final full-length campaign composition.\n\nThe same woman stands right of center in a three-quarter rear pose, looking toward the right horizon. Her complete trench coat occupies approximately two-thirds of the frame height, with both boots visible and naturally grounded. The left side remains open, showing uninterrupted blue twilight and dark volcanic terrain.\n\nThe coat has settled into a clear, elongated silhouette. Its shoulder line, belted waist, long sleeves, and substantial lower panels are fully readable. Only the hem edge and a few strands of hair continue to move gently.\n\nThe camera makes a very small, slow push forward and becomes still for the final second. Hold this composed product-focused image until the end of the 15-second video. Do not fade to black. Leave the negative space clean for later brand placement; generate no text, logo, subtitle, or watermark.\n\nThroughout the commercial, preserve the reference woman, garment, landscape, lighting direction, and restrained color palette. Use clean editorial cuts, not morphing transitions. Keep natural skin texture, realistic cloth weight, stable garment construction, and believable contact with the ground. No additional people, bags, jewelry, buildings, vehicles, floating garments, or studio product inserts. The trench coat remains the visual subject rather than becoming a minor detail in a landscape montage.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA continuous, spacious wind moves across the volcanic plain, with subtle stereo movement and no exaggerated roaring. Footsteps produce short, dry crunches synchronized with the boots, while close garment shots reveal soft woven-fabric movement. The wind rises during the sustained gust, then recedes into a q